       </table><p style="padding-bottom:1pt;font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;border-bottom:0.75pt solid;margin-right:93.333%;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:2pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">(1) - </span><ix:footnote id="FNT_bbbedd23-1fae-4c62-b746-93748a071a0f" xml:lang="en-US"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">Recorded within premiums earned on the Company's consolidated statements of operations.</span></ix:footnote><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:7pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> </span></p></ix:nonNumeric></div><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:12pt;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">As of December 31, 2025 and 2024</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">, the weighted average risk-free rates used to discount future installment premiums was </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_a077ed89-6dfe-48e6-8286-cd91623af756" contextRef="C_94b559e1-722d-431f-a464-3bd7e7523f59" name="us-gaap:FinancialGuaranteeInsuranceContractsPremiumReceivedOverContractPeriodPremiumReceivableWeightedAverageRiskFreeDiscountRate" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">3.1</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">% and </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_db8cb359-49e0-4b8b-b780-b47e2b90bf6b" contextRef="C_59c5d650-7bad-452f-b491-f323b4c8e259" name="us-gaap:FinancialGuaranteeInsuranceContractsPremiumReceivedOverContractPeriodPremiumReceivableWeightedAverageRiskFreeDiscountRate" unitRef="U_pure" scale="-2" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">3.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">%, respectively, and the weighted average expected collection term of the premiums receivable was </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_bb2ae51b-3035-4a74-a221-d7073668f296" contextRef="C_94b559e1-722d-431f-a464-3bd7e7523f59" name="us-gaap:FinancialGuaranteeInsuranceContractsPremiumReceivedOverContractPeriodPremiumReceivableWeightedAverageCollectionPeriod1" format="ixt-sec:duryear"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">8.33</span></ix:nonNumeric></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> years and </span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;"><ix:nonNumeric id="F_01bc92e0-46b4-431d-99e5-fe174b6477f5" contextRef="C_59c5d650-7bad-452f-b491-f323b4c8e259" name="us-gaap:FinancialGuaranteeInsuranceContractsPremiumReceivedOverContractPeriodPremiumReceivableWeightedAverageCollectionPeriod1" format="ixt-sec:duryear"><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">8.57</span></ix:nonNumeric></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> years, respectively. As of </span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">December 31, 2025 and 2024</span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">, reinsurance premiums payable was $</span><span style="font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"><ix:nonFraction id="F_6e7ad126-63c4-4cf1-8986-dcbf702b3b95" contextRef="C_188c5d8d-41e4-4dbf-b108-0be13d6108e0" name="us-gaap:ReinsurancePayable" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal"><ix:nonFraction id="F_153294ae-a37c-4c27-a168-b83c1dcdda29" contextRef="C_f4b26e79-33b7-4740-8a43-5b85821305d2" name="us-gaap:ReinsurancePayable" unitRef="U_USD" scale="6" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal">3</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#000000;white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;"> million and is included in &#8220;Other liabilities&#8221; in the Company&#8217;s consolidated balance sheets. The reinsurance premiums payable is accreted and paid to reinsurers as premiums due to MBIA are accreted and collected.</span></p><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p><p style="font-size:10pt;margin-top:0;font-family:Times New Roman;margin-bottom:0;text-align:left;"><span style="white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:10pt;font-family:Arial;font-kerning:none;min-width:fit-content;">&#160;</span></p